Parity with the web source (a pure presentational component; the hosting Security & Access page owns all fetching):
  * Title  -> SectionTitle "Window Status Detail" (web <h2 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-200>), exposed as a level-2 heading.
  * Layout -> TsFadeIn(delay 150ms == web delay={0.15}) over a responsive TsGrid(Columns=4, Gutter=16, ItemMinWidth=180)
              reproducing the web `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4` (collapses 4->2->1 by width).
  * 4 panels in the web WINDOW_KEYS order: fd "Front Driver", fp "Front Passenger", rd "Rear Driver", rp "Rear Passenger".
  * parseWindowState ported verbatim (asNonEmptyString guard: null/boolean/empty -> Unknown; "closed"/"0" -> Closed;
    contains "vent" -> Venting; any other non-empty string -> Open). Booleans collapse to Unknown exactly as the web helper.
  * windowColor / windowTextClass -> token brushes: Closed=Success(green), Venting=Warning(amber), Open=Danger(red),
    Unknown=TextMuted(gray). Each panel = TsGlassPanel(border=accent/40) + a /20 accent tint fill + bold accent value.
States rendered (the web source's real branches, reproduced exhaustively):
  Closed / Venting / Open / Unknown per panel + the no-data surface (a missing `latest` == WindowStatusDetailModel.Empty -> all 4 Unknown).
  The generic loading/error/stale/offline belong to the parent page (the web component never fetches), documented in the model XML-doc.
Accessibility: each panel carries a composed Narrator name ("Label: StateText"); decorative inner texts are AccessibilityView.Raw;
  title is a level-2 heading; TsFadeIn honours the OS reduce-motion setting; TextBlocks honour the system font scale.
i18n: every string flows through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade. translation.admin.security.windowDetail IS in the catalog
  (apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw). The window-label + windowState.* keys are inline-fallback-only - they are absent
